# L0441: `interrupt fn` / `naked fn` are freestanding-tier constructs.
#
# This module has no `no-runtime` directive, so it is compiled in the SAFE tier,
# which has a runtime: a host allocator, reference counting, an actor scheduler.
# A hardware entry point is meaningless there — the CPU's IDT does not vector into
# a hosted process, and the handler would run with none of the tier's invariants
# (it can interrupt the allocator mid-update, it cannot allocate, and it must not
# be entered by a `call`). §6 makes both kinds `L0441` outside the tier.
interrupt fn timer_isr frame ptr<i64>
    unsafe
        ptr_write(frame, 1)

fn main -> i64
    0
